                <pb facs="0734" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-15T20:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                                1921—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 16—5:53
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>57. The Shah sent for me this afternoon and expressed the hope that now that the
                    British financial advisers had definitely severed their connection with the
                    Persian Government it might be possible to obtain Americans to take their
                    places. His Majesty then reiterated some of the statements reported in the
                    Legation’s 35, June 21, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
